1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:04,694
Two thousand years ago, a
physician told an emperor:

2
00:00:04,694 --> 00:00:06,308
you are not a closed
machine.

3
00:00:06,308 --> 00:00:08,200
You are a body wired into
the sky.

4
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,006
Not astrology. Something
simpler.

5
00:00:13,006 --> 00:00:16,184
A body is a landscape, and
a landscape has weather.

6
00:00:16,184 --> 00:00:19,050
The force that guards it,
they called yang qi.

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,056
Yang qi is to your body
what the sun is to the sky.

8
00:00:25,056 --> 00:00:27,800
Four thieves come for it:
cold, heat, damp, wind.

9
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:33,825
And the text's most
startling word is

10
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:36,127
self-injury. Overwork it,
and it flares outward.

11
00:00:36,127 --> 00:00:37,950
Lose your temper, and it
turns on you.

12
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,040
The answer is almost
insultingly plain.

13
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,960
At dawn it rises, at noon it
peaks,

14
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:48,100
at dusk it draws inward.
So: go to bed.

15
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:53,329
When yin is level and yang
is sealed,

16
00:00:53,329 --> 00:00:56,157
the spirit is in order.
Fourteen characters.

17
00:00:56,157 --> 00:00:57,829
The Emperor's Inner
Canon.

18
00:00:57,829 --> 00:00:59,050
The Sun Inside You.
